`css/style.css` was overwritten with the PHP source of `index.php`, breaking all styling. A prior incomplete fix to `register.php` left the email uniqueness DB query running against a `null` value when email validation failed — the same class of bug as the `strlen(null)` TypeError fixed in PR #125, just never addressed for email.

## Changes

- **`css/style.css`** — Restored to correct CSS content. The file contained PHP/HTML from `index.php` instead of stylesheet rules.

- **`register.php`** — Wrapped the email uniqueness check in an `else` block, consistent with the username fix from PR #125:

```php
// Before: query ran unconditionally even when $_POST['email'] was null
if (empty($_POST['email'])) {
    $errors[] = 'You didn\'t enter a valid email address';
}
$db->query('SELECT COUNT(id) FROM users WHERE email = ?');
$db->execute([$_POST['email']]);  // null when validation failed

// After: mirrors the username guard pattern
if (empty($_POST['email'])) {
    $errors[] = 'You didn\'t enter a valid email address';
} else {
    $db->query('SELECT COUNT(id) FROM users WHERE email = ?');
    $db->execute([$_POST['email']]);
    if ($db->result()) {
        $errors[] = 'That email is already in use';
    }
}
```

