The local directory scanner unconditionally skipped all hidden entries (names starting with `.`), so a repo like `.github` was never recorded as present — causing it to land in `ManagedMissing` and trigger a clone attempt against an already-existing directory.

## Changes

- **`internal/scanner/scanner.go`**: tighten the hidden-entry skip to only apply to entries *not* in the managed repos map — dot-prefix repos are now processed through the normal classification path.

```go
// before
if len(name) > 0 && name[0] == '.' {
    continue
}

// after
if len(name) > 0 && name[0] == '.' {
    if _, ok := includedMap[name]; !ok {
        continue
    }
}
```

- **`internal/scanner/scanner_test.go`** *(new)*: three targeted cases — dot-prefix repo present and valid (→ `ManagedFound`), dot-prefix repo absent (→ `ManagedMissing`), and unmanaged hidden dirs (e.g. `.git` in the parent) still ignored.

